#11707
"Out On A Limb"
"You are in a courtyard with walls cobbled of rough-hewn, mica-flecked stone.
A profusion of pale violet wisteria climbs the enclosure, filling the air with
its sweet, heady fragrance.  Smooth river rocks create a path leading to a
round of flagstones laid in a spiral pattern, at the centre of which is a
carpet of green.  In the northwest corner a small spring burbles into a tiny
pool, spilling over gently to nourish the garden.  Growing nearby, a mimosa
tree lends shade and beauty with its delicate frothy blossoms.
"
